  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "2/1kWb16SH/uyiSXHJokG7kws+8=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:22.918Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Consileon is in the German Camunda cohort on the strength of its ranking and sector weighting, not on a verified deployment. The resolved facts are that it is a top-20 Lunendonk consultancy weighted towards banking and insurance; the Camunda attribution in its record is explicitly unverified.\n\nThat is a claim about the research state as much as about the firm. The cohort exists because a Camunda footprint implies a specific gap, and that argument only applies to firms that actually run Camunda. Consileon's membership is therefore a hypothesis about where to look, with the sector weighting as the reason the hypothesis is plausible: banking and insurance are where German process-engine density is expected to concentrate.\n\nThe practical consequence is ordering. Verification comes before outreach, because a pitch built on an orchestration gap fails immediately against a firm that does not have one. Priority 3 reflects that.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**3 \u00b7 later**\n- Consileon (DE)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> Top-20 Lunendonk, banking and insurance weighted.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:28:22.918343Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:28:22.918348Z"
    }
  },
